    <string-array name="bunny_facts">
        <item>A rabbit\'s teeth never stop growing, so they have to keep chewing to wear them down.</item>
        <item>A happy rabbit does a \"binky\": a jump with a twist in mid-air.</item>
        <item>Rabbits can see almost all the way around themselves, except for a small blind spot right in front of the nose.</item>
        <item>Rabbits can\'t vomit, so eating something bad is extra dangerous for them.</item>
        <item>A content rabbit \"purrs\" by gently grinding its teeth.</item>
        <item>Baby rabbits are called kits.</item>
        <item>Rabbits are most active at dawn and dusk.</item>
        <item>Those big ears also work as radiators and help a rabbit cool down.</item>
        <item>A group of rabbits is sometimes called a fluffle.</item>
        <item>A thumping rabbit is warning everyone nearby that something seems off.</item>
    </string-array>
